{"name":"Scented Candle","hex":"#907361","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scented","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pleasant aroma.","Having a smell of any kind."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of scent"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scented"},{"term":"candle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light source consisting of a wick embedded in a solid, flammable substance such as wax, tallow, or paraffin.","The protruding, removable portion of a filter, particularly a water filter."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To observe the growth of an embryo inside (an egg), using a bright light source.","To dry (greenware) prior to the firing cycle, setting the kiln at 200° Celsius until all water is removed from the greenware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candle","blocks":[{"text":"A candle is an ignitable wick embedded in wax, or another flammable solid substance such as tallow, that provides light, and in some cases, a fragrance. A candle can also provide heat or a method of keeping time. Candles have been used for over two millennia around the world, and were a significant form of indoor lighting until the invention of other types of light sources. Although electric light has largely made candle use nonessential for illumination, candles are still commonly used for functional, symbolic and aesthetic purposes and in specific cultural and religious settings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg/330px-LA2_Skultuna_kontorsljusstake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Always.gif/330px-Always.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thum